# <%= projectName %> Patterns Catalog

**Purpose:** A curated register of reusable code patterns surveyed from this repository.
Each entry is anchored to a literal directory under `src/` (or the project's source root) and
answers the same six questions, so a contributor can decide reuse-vs-new without reading code.

**Location:** `docs/METHOD/PATTERNS_CATALOG.md`
**Spec:** `docs/METHOD/REUSE_REGISTRY_SPEC.md` (the CANON-16 existing-code survey protocol)

Read this — and search `REUSE_REGISTRY.md` — before opening a new file under `src/`.
This register is owned by the project: `arbiter update` never overwrites it once it exists.

---

## Purpose

The catalog names the patterns worth reusing so they are extended, not re-invented. It is not a
tutorial: each entry is a pointer plus the design decisions worth knowing before you copy it.

---

## Entry schema

Each entry is a level-2 heading `## <n>. <pattern name>` followed by six labelled fields:

- **Use when:** the situation the pattern is the right answer to.
- **Avoid when:** the situation where reaching for it is a mistake.
- **Registry path:** the literal directory the pattern lives in, in backticks (no globs).
- **Variation axis:** what legitimately differs between instances of the pattern.
- **Test approach:** how instances of the pattern are tested.
- **Rejected alternatives:** the design that was considered and dropped, and why.

Keep the catalog small (a dozen entries at most): it lists load-bearing patterns, not every helper.

---

## Catalog

_No patterns catalogued yet._ Add the first entry when a reusable pattern emerges — a shape that
appears in two or more places and is worth surveying before writing a third. Record the survey in
your plan per `REUSE_REGISTRY_SPEC.md`.
